NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sometimes you need to attach your own arbitrary data or functions to a table or its columns so that they are available anywhere the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column"},{"type":"text","value":" instances are available. That is what the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" options are for. TanStack Table never reads or writes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" itself; it is purely a place for you to pass your own context through the table."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two kinds of meta:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table meta"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" table option. Pass any object and read it back anywhere via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.options.meta"},{"type":"text","value":". A classic use case is passing an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateData"},{"type":"text","value":" function down to editable cells."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column meta"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" property on a column definition. Read it back anywhere a column is available via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.columnDef.meta"},{"type":"text","value":". A classic use case is declaring which filter UI variant a column's header should render."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Meta"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"ember"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"table = useTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"lit"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = this.tableController.table({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"alpine"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return local.data\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside an Alpine.data method)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vanilla"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"const table = constructTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)","lang":"ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"preact\",\"octane\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"angular\",\"ember\",\"lit\",\"alpine\",\"vanilla\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = useTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"preact\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = useTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"octane\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = useTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"vue\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = useTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = createTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  get data() {\\n    return data()\\n  },\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"svelte\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = createTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  get data() {\\n    return data\\n  },\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"angular\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data: this.data(),\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n}))\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"ember\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"table = useTable(() => ({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data: this.data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n}))\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"lit\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = this.tableController.table({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data: this.data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"alpine\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = createTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  get data() {\\n    return local.data\\n  },\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside an Alpine.data method)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"vanilla\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"const table = constructTable({\\n  features,\\n  columns,\\n  data,\\n  meta: {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\\n      // ...\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\\n\\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column meta is set on the column definition and is identical across every adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    meta: {\n      filterVariant: 'range',\n    },\n  }),\n])\n\n// ...later, anywhere a column is available (e.g. inside a header component)\nconst variant = column.columnDef.meta?.filterVariant","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typing-meta-per-table-recommended","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typing Meta Per-Table (Recommended)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, both meta types are empty objects, so to get type safety you declare their shapes yourself. New in v9, you can declare meta types "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per feature set"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the type-only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slots in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":" call, using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metaHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" utility."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First, define the shapes you want (this is the same in every framework):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface MyTableMeta {\n  updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n}\n\ninterface MyColumnMeta {\n  filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then declare them on your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/preact-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"ember"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"lit"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"alpine"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vanilla"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\nimport { storeReactivityBindings } from '@tanstack/table-core/store-reactivity-bindings'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  coreReactivityFeature: storeReactivityBindings(),\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"preact\",\"octane\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"angular\",\"ember\",\"lit\",\"alpine\",\"vanilla\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"preact\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/preact-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"octane\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/octane-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"vue\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"svelte\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"angular\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"ember\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"lit\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"alpine\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"vanilla\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import {\\n  metaHelper,\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableFeatures,\\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\\nimport { storeReactivityBindings } from '@tanstack/table-core/store-reactivity-bindings'\\n\\nconst features = tableFeatures({\\n  coreReactivityFeature: storeReactivityBindings(),\\n  rowSortingFeature,\\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\\n})\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That's it. Everywhere this "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object flows ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTable"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnDef"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Column"},{"type":"text","value":", and so on), the meta types are inferred from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"},{"type":"text","value":" with no extra generics to pass around:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n  meta: {\n    filterVariant: 'range', // ✅ type-checked against MyColumnMeta\n  },\n})\n\n// And both meta surfaces are fully typed wherever you read them:\ntable.options.meta?.updateData // ✅ (rowIndex, columnId, value) => void\ncolumn.columnDef.meta?.filterVariant // ✅ 'text' | 'range' | 'select' | undefined","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unlike the v8-style declaration merging described below, this scoping is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per-table, not global"}]},{"type":"text","value":": only tables created with this "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object get these meta types. Different tables in your app can declare entirely different meta shapes by using different "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" objects."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"how-the-type-only-slots-work","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How the Type-Only Slots Work"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" keys are "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"phantom"}]},{"type":"text","value":" entries. Only their TypeScript types matter. At runtime, the value is an empty object that gets stripped from the table's registered features, so it is never treated as a real feature. The actual meta "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"values"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are still passed where they always were: the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" table option and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" property on column definitions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metaHelper<MyMeta>()"},{"type":"text","value":" simply returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":" cast to your meta type. You can write the cast yourself instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: {} as MyTableMeta,\n  columnMeta: {} as MyColumnMeta,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both forms are equivalent. Prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metaHelper"},{"type":"text","value":". It reads as type-only at a glance, and it avoids false positives from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@typescript-eslint/no-unnecessary-type-assertion"},{"type":"text","value":" lint rule, which flags the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{} as"},{"type":"text","value":" form when your meta type has only optional properties (and whose auto-fix would silently erase your meta type)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"filter-meta-filtermeta-slot","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filter Meta ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" Slot)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slot lets you declare the shape of arbitrary metadata that a custom filter function attaches to a row during filtering. This is most useful for filter functions that produce a by-product (such as a ranking score) that you want to read in a column's sort function or cell renderer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pattern mirrors "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":": declare your meta interface, register it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metaHelper"},{"type":"text","value":", and then intersect "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" with your meta type when annotating your filter and sort functions."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  metaHelper,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  globalFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport type {\n  FilterFn,\n  SortFn,\n  RowData,\n  TableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport { rankItem, type RankingInfo } from '@tanstack/match-sorter-utils'\n\n// 1. Define the metadata shape your filter function will attach\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\n// 2. Intersect with TableFeatures to get a fully typed features surface\ntype FuzzyFeatures = TableFeatures & { filterMeta: FuzzyFilterMeta }\n\n// 3. Annotate your filter and sort functions against the extended features type\nconst fuzzyFilter: FilterFn<FuzzyFeatures, RowData> = (\n  row,\n  columnId,\n  value,\n  addMeta,\n) => {\n  const itemRank = rankItem(row.getValue(columnId), value)\n  addMeta({ itemRank })\n  return itemRank.passed\n}\n\nconst fuzzySort: SortFn<FuzzyFeatures, Person> = (rowA, rowB, columnId) => {\n  let dir = 0\n  if (rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]) {\n    dir = compareItems(\n      rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]?.itemRank!,\n      rowB.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]?.itemRank!,\n    )\n  }\n  return dir === 0 ? sortFn_alphanumeric(rowA, rowB, columnId) : dir\n}\n\n// 4. Register everything on tableFeatures(), including the filterMeta slot\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  globalFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  sortFns: { fuzzy: fuzzySort },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":" slots above register only the functions this table uses. The full built-in registries ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" exported from the package) can still be spread into these slots, but they are deprecated because they put every built-in function in your bundle. Import individual functions such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn_alphanumeric"},{"type":"text","value":" instead, or pass functions directly in your column definitions."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnFiltersMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" on every row is typed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FuzzyFilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" for tables built from this "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slot is, like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":", a phantom type-only entry. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":" at runtime and is stripped from the registered features."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/examples/filters-fuzzy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React filters-fuzzy example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a complete, runnable implementation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typing-meta-globally-with-declaration-merging-v8-style","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typing Meta Globally with Declaration Merging (v8 Style)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v8 approach of extending the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" interfaces with module augmentation still works in v9. The only change from v8 is the generics shape: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" is now the first type parameter on both interfaces."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/preact-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/preact-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/octane-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/svelte-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"ember"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/ember-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"lit"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"alpine"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/alpine-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vanilla"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/table-core'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"preact\",\"octane\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"angular\",\"ember\",\"lit\",\"alpine\",\"vanilla\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/react-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"preact\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/preact-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/preact-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"octane\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/octane-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"vue\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"svelte\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/svelte-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"angular\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"ember\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/ember-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"lit\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"alpine\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/alpine-table' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"vanilla\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/table-core'\\n\\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\\n  }\\n\\n  interface ColumnMeta<\\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\\n    TData extends RowData,\\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\\n  > {\\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The trade-off with declaration merging is that it is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"global"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Every table in your entire project gets the same meta types, whether or not a given table actually provides that meta. If you have many tables with different needs, the per-table slots above are a better fit."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The two approaches resolve with a simple precedence: if a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object declares a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slot, that slot's type is used for tables created with those features, "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replacing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (not merging with) the globally declared interface. Tables whose features declare no slot fall back to the declaration-merged interfaces."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-custom-features-instead","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to Use Custom Features Instead"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meta is intentionally simple: a typed bag of values you carry through the table. If you find yourself wanting real table "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with defaults, new "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state"}]},{"type":"text","value":", or new "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"APIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on the table instance (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.toggleDensity()"},{"type":"text","value":"), consider writing a "},{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/guide/custom-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom feature"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instead. Custom features plug into the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option, get the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"},{"type":"text","value":" type inference, and can declare their own options, state, and instance methods. Meta was never designed to do any of that."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"table-meta","text":"Table Meta","level":2},{"id":"typing-meta-per-table-recommended","text":"Typing Meta Per-Table (Recommended)","level":2},{"id":"how-the-type-only-slots-work","text":"How the Type-Only Slots Work","level":3},{"id":"filter-meta-filtermeta-slot","text":"Filter Meta (filterMeta Slot)","level":2},{"id":"typing-meta-globally-with-declaration-merging-v8-style","text":"Typing Meta Globally with Declaration Merging (v8 Style)","level":2},{"id":"when-to-use-custom-features-instead","text":"When to Use Custom Features Instead","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","preact","octane","vue","solid","svelte","angular","ember","lit","alpine","vanilla"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSometimes you need to attach your own arbitrary data or functions to a table or its columns so that they are available anywhere the `table` or `column` instances are available. That is what the `meta` options are for. TanStack Table never reads or writes `meta` itself; it is purely a place for you to pass your own context through the table.\n\nThere are two kinds of meta:\n\n- **Table meta** - The `meta` table option. Pass any object and read it back anywhere via `table.options.meta`. A classic use case is passing an `updateData` function down to editable cells.\n- **Column meta** - The `meta` property on a column definition. Read it back anywhere a column is available via `column.columnDef.meta`. A classic use case is declaring which filter UI variant a column's header should render.\n\n## Table Meta\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n```ts\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n```ts\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Ember\n\n```ts\ntable = useTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Lit\n\n```ts\nconst table = this.tableController.table({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Alpine\n\n```ts\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return local.data\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside an Alpine.data method)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Vanilla\n\n```ts\nconst table = constructTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nColumn meta is set on the column definition and is identical across every adapter:\n\n```ts\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    meta: {\n      filterVariant: 'range',\n    },\n  }),\n])\n\n// ...later, anywhere a column is available (e.g. inside a header component)\nconst variant = column.columnDef.meta?.filterVariant\n```\n\n## Typing Meta Per-Table (Recommended)\n\nBy default, both meta types are empty objects, so to get type safety you declare their shapes yourself. New in v9, you can declare meta types **per feature set** with the type-only `tableMeta` and `columnMeta` slots in your `tableFeatures()` call, using the `metaHelper` utility.\n\nFirst, define the shapes you want (this is the same in every framework):\n\n```ts\ninterface MyTableMeta {\n  updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n}\n\ninterface MyColumnMeta {\n  filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n}\n```\n\nThen declare them on your `features` object:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/preact-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Ember\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Lit\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Alpine\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Vanilla\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\nimport { storeReactivityBindings } from '@tanstack/table-core/store-reactivity-bindings'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  coreReactivityFeature: storeReactivityBindings(),\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThat's it. Everywhere this `features` object flows (`useTable`, `createColumnHelper`, `ColumnDef`, `Column`, and so on), the meta types are inferred from `typeof features` with no extra generics to pass around:\n\n```ts\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n  meta: {\n    filterVariant: 'range', // ✅ type-checked against MyColumnMeta\n  },\n})\n\n// And both meta surfaces are fully typed wherever you read them:\ntable.options.meta?.updateData // ✅ (rowIndex, columnId, value) => void\ncolumn.columnDef.meta?.filterVariant // ✅ 'text' | 'range' | 'select' | undefined\n```\n\nUnlike the v8-style declaration merging described below, this scoping is **per-table, not global**: only tables created with this `features` object get these meta types. Different tables in your app can declare entirely different meta shapes by using different `features` objects.\n\n### How the Type-Only Slots Work\n\nThe `tableMeta` and `columnMeta` keys are _phantom_ entries. Only their TypeScript types matter. At runtime, the value is an empty object that gets stripped from the table's registered features, so it is never treated as a real feature. The actual meta _values_ are still passed where they always were: the `meta` table option and the `meta` property on column definitions.\n\n`metaHelper<MyMeta>()` simply returns `{}` cast to your meta type. You can write the cast yourself instead:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: {} as MyTableMeta,\n  columnMeta: {} as MyColumnMeta,\n})\n```\n\nBoth forms are equivalent. Prefer `metaHelper`. It reads as type-only at a glance, and it avoids false positives from the `@typescript-eslint/no-unnecessary-type-assertion` lint rule, which flags the `{} as` form when your meta type has only optional properties (and whose auto-fix would silently erase your meta type).\n\n## Filter Meta (`filterMeta` Slot)\n\nThe `filterMeta` slot lets you declare the shape of arbitrary metadata that a custom filter function attaches to a row during filtering. This is most useful for filter functions that produce a by-product (such as a ranking score) that you want to read in a column's sort function or cell renderer.\n\nThe pattern mirrors `tableMeta` and `columnMeta`: declare your meta interface, register it with `metaHelper`, and then intersect `TableFeatures` with your meta type when annotating your filter and sort functions.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  globalFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport type {\n  FilterFn,\n  SortFn,\n  RowData,\n  TableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport { rankItem, type RankingInfo } from '@tanstack/match-sorter-utils'\n\n// 1. Define the metadata shape your filter function will attach\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\n// 2. Intersect with TableFeatures to get a fully typed features surface\ntype FuzzyFeatures = TableFeatures & { filterMeta: FuzzyFilterMeta }\n\n// 3. Annotate your filter and sort functions against the extended features type\nconst fuzzyFilter: FilterFn<FuzzyFeatures, RowData> = (\n  row,\n  columnId,\n  value,\n  addMeta,\n) => {\n  const itemRank = rankItem(row.getValue(columnId), value)\n  addMeta({ itemRank })\n  return itemRank.passed\n}\n\nconst fuzzySort: SortFn<FuzzyFeatures, Person> = (rowA, rowB, columnId) => {\n  let dir = 0\n  if (rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]) {\n    dir = compareItems(\n      rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]?.itemRank!,\n      rowB.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]?.itemRank!,\n    )\n  }\n  return dir === 0 ? sortFn_alphanumeric(rowA, rowB, columnId) : dir\n}\n\n// 4. Register everything on tableFeatures(), including the filterMeta slot\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  globalFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  sortFns: { fuzzy: fuzzySort },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> the `filterFns` and `sortFns` slots above register only the functions this table uses. The full built-in registries (`filterFns`, `sortFns`, `aggregationFns` exported from the package) can still be spread into these slots, but they are deprecated because they put every built-in function in your bundle. Import individual functions such as `sortFn_alphanumeric` instead, or pass functions directly in your column definitions.\n\nNow `columnFiltersMeta` on every row is typed as `FuzzyFilterMeta` for tables built from this `features` object. The `filterMeta` slot is, like `tableMeta` and `columnMeta`, a phantom type-only entry. `metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>()` returns `{}` at runtime and is stripped from the registered features.\n\nSee the [React filters-fuzzy example](../framework/react/examples/filters-fuzzy) for a complete, runnable implementation.\n\n## Typing Meta Globally with Declaration Merging (v8 Style)\n\nThe v8 approach of extending the `TableMeta` and `ColumnMeta` interfaces with module augmentation still works in v9. The only change from v8 is the generics shape: `TFeatures` is now the first type parameter on both interfaces.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/preact-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/preact-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/octane-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/svelte-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Ember\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/ember-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Lit\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Alpine\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/alpine-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Vanilla\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/table-core'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThe trade-off with declaration merging is that it is **global**. Every table in your entire project gets the same meta types, whether or not a given table actually provides that meta. If you have many tables with different needs, the per-table slots above are a better fit.\n\nThe two approaches resolve with a simple precedence: if a `features` object declares a `tableMeta` or `columnMeta` slot, that slot's type is used for tables created with those features, _replacing_ (not merging with) the globally declared interface. Tables whose features declare no slot fall back to the declaration-merged interfaces.\n\n## When to Use Custom Features Instead\n\nMeta is intentionally simple: a typed bag of values you carry through the table. If you find yourself wanting real table _options_ with defaults, new _state_, or new _APIs_ on the table instance (e.g. `table.toggleDensity()`), consider writing a [custom feature](../framework/react/guide/custom-features) instead. Custom features plug into the same `features` option, get the same `typeof features` type inference, and can declare their own options, state, and instance methods. Meta was never designed to do any of that.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Table and Column Meta Guide\n---\n\nSometimes you need to attach your own arbitrary data or functions to a table or its columns so that they are available anywhere the `table` or `column` instances are available. That is what the `meta` options are for. TanStack Table never reads or writes `meta` itself; it is purely a place for you to pass your own context through the table.\n\nThere are two kinds of meta:\n\n- **Table meta** - The `meta` table option. Pass any object and read it back anywhere via `table.options.meta`. A classic use case is passing an `updateData` function down to editable cells.\n- **Column meta** - The `meta` property on a column definition. Read it back anywhere a column is available via `column.columnDef.meta`. A classic use case is declaring which filter UI variant a column's header should render.\n\n## Table Meta\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n```ts\nconst table = useTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data()\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n```ts\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return data\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n```ts\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Ember\n\n```ts\ntable = useTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n}))\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Lit\n\n```ts\nconst table = this.tableController.table({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: this.data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Alpine\n\n```ts\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return local.data\n  },\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside an Alpine.data method)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n# Vanilla\n\n```ts\nconst table = constructTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n  meta: {\n    updateData: (rowIndex, columnId, value) => {\n      // ...\n    },\n  },\n})\n\n// ...later, anywhere the table is available (e.g. inside a cell component)\ntable.options.meta?.updateData(rowIndex, columnId, newValue)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nColumn meta is set on the column definition and is identical across every adapter:\n\n```ts\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    meta: {\n      filterVariant: 'range',\n    },\n  }),\n])\n\n// ...later, anywhere a column is available (e.g. inside a header component)\nconst variant = column.columnDef.meta?.filterVariant\n```\n\n## Typing Meta Per-Table (Recommended)\n\nBy default, both meta types are empty objects, so to get type safety you declare their shapes yourself. New in v9, you can declare meta types **per feature set** with the type-only `tableMeta` and `columnMeta` slots in your `tableFeatures()` call, using the `metaHelper` utility.\n\nFirst, define the shapes you want (this is the same in every framework):\n\n```ts\ninterface MyTableMeta {\n  updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n}\n\ninterface MyColumnMeta {\n  filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n}\n```\n\nThen declare them on your `features` object:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/preact-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Ember\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Lit\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Alpine\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n# Vanilla\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\nimport { storeReactivityBindings } from '@tanstack/table-core/store-reactivity-bindings'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  coreReactivityFeature: storeReactivityBindings(),\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: metaHelper<MyTableMeta>(),\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<MyColumnMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThat's it. Everywhere this `features` object flows (`useTable`, `createColumnHelper`, `ColumnDef`, `Column`, and so on), the meta types are inferred from `typeof features` with no extra generics to pass around:\n\n```ts\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n  meta: {\n    filterVariant: 'range', // ✅ type-checked against MyColumnMeta\n  },\n})\n\n// And both meta surfaces are fully typed wherever you read them:\ntable.options.meta?.updateData // ✅ (rowIndex, columnId, value) => void\ncolumn.columnDef.meta?.filterVariant // ✅ 'text' | 'range' | 'select' | undefined\n```\n\nUnlike the v8-style declaration merging described below, this scoping is **per-table, not global**: only tables created with this `features` object get these meta types. Different tables in your app can declare entirely different meta shapes by using different `features` objects.\n\n### How the Type-Only Slots Work\n\nThe `tableMeta` and `columnMeta` keys are _phantom_ entries. Only their TypeScript types matter. At runtime, the value is an empty object that gets stripped from the table's registered features, so it is never treated as a real feature. The actual meta _values_ are still passed where they always were: the `meta` table option and the `meta` property on column definitions.\n\n`metaHelper<MyMeta>()` simply returns `{}` cast to your meta type. You can write the cast yourself instead:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  tableMeta: {} as MyTableMeta,\n  columnMeta: {} as MyColumnMeta,\n})\n```\n\nBoth forms are equivalent. Prefer `metaHelper`. It reads as type-only at a glance, and it avoids false positives from the `@typescript-eslint/no-unnecessary-type-assertion` lint rule, which flags the `{} as` form when your meta type has only optional properties (and whose auto-fix would silently erase your meta type).\n\n## Filter Meta (`filterMeta` Slot)\n\nThe `filterMeta` slot lets you declare the shape of arbitrary metadata that a custom filter function attaches to a row during filtering. This is most useful for filter functions that produce a by-product (such as a ranking score) that you want to read in a column's sort function or cell renderer.\n\nThe pattern mirrors `tableMeta` and `columnMeta`: declare your meta interface, register it with `metaHelper`, and then intersect `TableFeatures` with your meta type when annotating your filter and sort functions.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  metaHelper,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  globalFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport type {\n  FilterFn,\n  SortFn,\n  RowData,\n  TableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/react-table'\nimport { rankItem, type RankingInfo } from '@tanstack/match-sorter-utils'\n\n// 1. Define the metadata shape your filter function will attach\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\n// 2. Intersect with TableFeatures to get a fully typed features surface\ntype FuzzyFeatures = TableFeatures & { filterMeta: FuzzyFilterMeta }\n\n// 3. Annotate your filter and sort functions against the extended features type\nconst fuzzyFilter: FilterFn<FuzzyFeatures, RowData> = (\n  row,\n  columnId,\n  value,\n  addMeta,\n) => {\n  const itemRank = rankItem(row.getValue(columnId), value)\n  addMeta({ itemRank })\n  return itemRank.passed\n}\n\nconst fuzzySort: SortFn<FuzzyFeatures, Person> = (rowA, rowB, columnId) => {\n  let dir = 0\n  if (rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]) {\n    dir = compareItems(\n      rowA.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]?.itemRank!,\n      rowB.columnFiltersMeta[columnId]?.itemRank!,\n    )\n  }\n  return dir === 0 ? sortFn_alphanumeric(rowA, rowB, columnId) : dir\n}\n\n// 4. Register everything on tableFeatures(), including the filterMeta slot\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  globalFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  sortFns: { fuzzy: fuzzySort },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> the `filterFns` and `sortFns` slots above register only the functions this table uses. The full built-in registries (`filterFns`, `sortFns`, `aggregationFns` exported from the package) can still be spread into these slots, but they are deprecated because they put every built-in function in your bundle. Import individual functions such as `sortFn_alphanumeric` instead, or pass functions directly in your column definitions.\n\nNow `columnFiltersMeta` on every row is typed as `FuzzyFilterMeta` for tables built from this `features` object. The `filterMeta` slot is, like `tableMeta` and `columnMeta`, a phantom type-only entry. `metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>()` returns `{}` at runtime and is stripped from the registered features.\n\nSee the [React filters-fuzzy example](../framework/react/examples/filters-fuzzy) for a complete, runnable implementation.\n\n## Typing Meta Globally with Declaration Merging (v8 Style)\n\nThe v8 approach of extending the `TableMeta` and `ColumnMeta` interfaces with module augmentation still works in v9. The only change from v8 is the generics shape: `TFeatures` is now the first type parameter on both interfaces.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/react-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Preact\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/preact-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/preact-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Octane\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/octane-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/octane-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Vue\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/vue-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/solid-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/svelte-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Angular\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Ember\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/ember-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/ember-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Lit\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Alpine\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/alpine-table' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Vanilla\n\n```ts\nimport type { CellData, RowData, TableFeatures } from '@tanstack/table-core'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface TableMeta<TFeatures extends TableFeatures, TData extends RowData> {\n    updateData: (rowIndex: number, columnId: string, value: unknown) => void\n  }\n\n  interface ColumnMeta<\n    TFeatures extends TableFeatures,\n    TData extends RowData,\n    TValue extends CellData = CellData,\n  > {\n    filterVariant?: 'text' | 'range' | 'select'\n  }\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThe trade-off with declaration merging is that it is **global**. Every table in your entire project gets the same meta types, whether or not a given table actually provides that meta. If you have many tables with different needs, the per-table slots above are a better fit.\n\nThe two approaches resolve with a simple precedence: if a `features` object declares a `tableMeta` or `columnMeta` slot, that slot's type is used for tables created with those features, _replacing_ (not merging with) the globally declared interface. Tables whose features declare no slot fall back to the declaration-merged interfaces.\n\n## When to Use Custom Features Instead\n\nMeta is intentionally simple: a typed bag of values you carry through the table. If you find yourself wanting real table _options_ with defaults, new _state_, or new _APIs_ on the table instance (e.g. `table.toggleDensity()`), consider writing a [custom feature](../framework/react/guide/custom-features) instead. Custom features plug into the same `features` option, get the same `typeof features` type inference, and can declare their own options, state, and instance methods. Meta was never designed to do any of that.\n"}
